   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "-eZ-rNGOp0kB",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "-eZ-rNGOp0kB"
   },
   "source": [
    "## DQA\n",
    "CRSElapsedTime shows a minimum of -60.0 which is physically impossible for flight time.\n",
    "\n",
    ">A negative scheduled flight duration is impossible. It means the scheduled arrival time appears to be before the scheduled departure time in the raw data. This happens in two known situations\n",
    "Exclude CRSElapsedTime as a feature since it carries this corruption. Dataset already have Distance and CRSDepTime/CRSArrTime covering similar signal.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "DdJ4gUsrseNT",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "DdJ4gUsrseNT",
    "outputId": "04399369-4819-4683-fb1a-10b34b3d4177"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Columns remaining: 16\n",
      "Columns: ['FlightDate', 'Year', 'Quarter', 'Month', 'DayofMonth', 'DayOfWeek', 'Marketing_Airline_Network', 'Operating_Airline', 'Origin', 'Dest', 'Distance', 'DistanceGroup', 'CRSDepTime', 'CRSArrTime', 'DepTimeBlk', 'ArrDel15']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Drop CRSElapsedTime, it contains impossible negative values (-292 min)\n",
    "# Distance and CRSDepTime/CRSArrTime carry the same signal cleanly\n",
    "\n",
    "df = df.drop(columns=['CRSElapsedTime'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Columns remaining: {df.shape[1]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Columns: {list(df.columns)}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "feature-selection-header",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "feature-selection-header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 2. Feature Selection: Process, rationale and methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Covers: leakage removal, candidate feature identification, statistical selection, final feature set justification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "leakage-guard-md",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "leakage-guard-md"
   },
   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Step 1: Remove leakage variables\n",
    "These columns reveal the answer (arrival delay) directly or are only known *after* landing. They are excluded before any modeling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "leakage-drop",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "leakage-drop",
    "outputId": "19728980-d735-4e00-d4ce-28cc85260750"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Target variable class distribution:\n",
      "ArrDel15\n",
      "0.0    0.81\n",
      "1.0    0.19\n",
      "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n",
      "\n",
      "Features remaining after leakage removal: 15\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Columns that cause data leakage, known only AFTER the flight lands\n",
    "LEAKAGE_COLS = [\n",
    "    'ArrDelay', 'ArrDel15',          # Target proxy, direct leakage\n",
    "    'ArrTime', 'ActualElapsedTime',   # Post-arrival info\n",
    "    'AirTime', 'WheelsOn', 'TaxiIn', # Post-arrival operational\n",
    "    'ArrivalDelayGroups', 'ArrTimeBlk',\n",
    "    'Cancelled', 'Diverted',          # If flight is cancelled/diverted, no ArrDel15\n",
    "    # Other Post-departure variable (shall be considered for removal when predicting EXACTLY BEFORE departure):\n",
    "    # 'DepDelay', 'DepDel15', 'TaxiOut', 'WheelsOff', 'DepTime'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "TARGET = 'ArrDel15'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Separate target before dropping\n",
    "y = df[TARGET].copy()\n",
    "X_raw = df.drop(columns=LEAKAGE_COLS + [col for col in LEAKAGE_COLS if col != TARGET], errors='ignore')\n",
    "\n",
