    "## Demo prediction remarks\n",
    "\n",
    ">We input a real-world flight scenario; American Airlines (AA) from San Francisco (SFO) to Los Angeles (LAX) on April 26th, Sunday, departing at 10:15 AM with an estimated arrival of 11:48 AM. 
     "The model predicts this flight arrives on time, with a delay probability of 32.7% 
     "A 32.7% delay probability means roughly 1 in 3 flights on this profile would still arrive late. 
     "An airline managing hundreds of similar flights daily would see that translate to meaningful operational impact.\n",
    ">Our model does not just say delayed or on time, it gives a probability score. An airline can set its own intervention threshold based on operational cost tolerance."
